        "note": "Road-limit estimates from the pinned Environment Agency one-metre last-return laser-intensity raster captured 6 January–5 February 2020, checked against native classified ground returns and satellite context. This grayscale survey records reflected laser energy, not RGB photography. Driver-left and driver-right limits follow the visible paved road and exclude roofs, field lanes, trees and hedges. Most anchor gaps are approximately 36 m. The wooded interval between stations 200 and 232 (approximately 96 m) is interpolated between the adjoining observations; canopy and sparse ground returns prevent a continuous edge survey there. The corrected source trace and supplied timing positions remain exact. The sparse final source endpoint is 38.5 m beyond the supplied finish; this preview follows the provisional source extent and is not an exact timed-course simulation. Native one-metre pixels, coordinate transformation, vegetation and interpolation limit accuracy. The existing raster terrain is retained; banking is unknown and rendered curbs illustrative.",
